<title>USA: Capitol Multimedia Q2 net loss from profit.</title>
<headline>Capitol Multimedia Q2 net loss from profit.</headline>
<dateline>BETHESDA, Md. 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended     Six Months Ended</p>
<p>			     Sep	  30	    Sep	   30</p>
<p>			    1996	1995	  1996	  1995</p>
<p>	   ----- (unaudited)     ----- ----- (unaudited) -----</p>
<p> Net sales	   327,161  1,059,162   1,339,710   2,455,343</p>
<p>Consolidation charges</p>
<p>			 462,566	    -     462,566	     -</p>
<p>Operating income</p>
<p>  (loss)	 (1,102,438)     75,130  (1,066,301)    (9,494)</p>
<p>Net income (loss)</p>
<p>		   (1,026,772)  2,660,915   (945,032)   2,691,414</p>
<p>Net income (loss)</p>
<p>  per share	    (.21)	  .48	 (.20)	   .49</p>
<p>Weighted average</p>
<p>shares outstanding</p>
<p>		     4,832,065  5,650,842   4,832,065   5,645,442</p>
<p>NOTE: Full name of company is Capitol Multimedia Inc.</p>
<p>The company attributed poor results for the 1996 period to problems in their industry, including a glut of CD-ROM titles, intense competition for children's animated story and adventure titles, suffering software development revenues as publishers cut back on 1997 title development.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
